  "body": "The [define the static attributes](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#define-the-static-attributes) algorithm describes its _definition_ parameter as an “interface or namespace”. Namespaces cannot have static attributes, though, and the algorithm is only ever invoked with interface definitions as _definition_ arguments, so this appears to be a mistake.\r\n\r\nThe same mistake repeats in [define the unforgeable regular attributes](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#define-the-unforgeable-regular-attributes). The [`[LegacyUnforgeable]`](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#LegacyUnforgeable) extended attribute isn’t applicable to attributes that are members of namespaces and the algorithm is again only invoked with interface definitions.",
